# 1. NON-NEGOTIABLE TECHNICAL CONSTRAINTS

Use ONLY:

- HTML5
- CSS3
- Vanilla JavaScript
- Browser `localStorage` for persistent data
- Chart.js through a CDN, if charts are useful
- Other small CDN libraries only when genuinely necessary and compatible with the beginner-track rules

Do NOT use:

- React
- Next.js
- Vue
- Angular
- Svelte
- TypeScript
- Tailwind CSS
- Bootstrap
- Node.js
- Express
- A backend server
- A database server
- A build system or framework

The application must run as a straightforward collection of HTML, CSS, and JavaScript files.

Use the following architecture:

```text
hcm-lite/
├── index.html
├── admin.html
├── employees.html
├── leaves.html
├── settings.html
├── employee.html
├── payslip.html
├── css/
│   └── style.css
├── js/
│   ├── storage.js
│   ├── auth.js
│   ├── employees.js
│   ├── attendance.js
│   ├── leave.js
│   ├── helper.js
│   ├── dashboard.js
│   ├── settings.js
│   └── payslip.js
├── assets/
├── README.md
└── .gitignore
```

You may add small, clearly named JavaScript files if necessary, but keep the project simple and understandable.

Reuse shared functions rather than duplicating logic across pages.

Do not convert this into a full-stack application. A real backend, real database, and hosted LLM integration are not required for this track.

Important limitation: `localStorage` is browser-specific and is not secure against someone who can inspect or modify the browser's data. Treat this as a learning project, do not store real sensitive employee information, and do not describe it as production-secure.

