# 7. ATTENDANCE MANAGEMENT

Implement actual check-in and check-out functionality.

### Check-in

- The employee can check in only once per working day.
- Store the date and time.
- Calculate status using the Admin's office start time and grace period.
- Prevent duplicate records.
- Update the employee dashboard and Admin attendance view.

### Check-out

- A check-out is allowed only after a check-in.
- Prevent duplicate or invalid check-outs.
- Calculate working duration.
- Mark a half day when total working duration is less than five hours, following the brief's rules.
- Update the stored record.

### Status rules

The brief defines:
- Late when check-in is after office start time plus grace minutes.
- One check-in per employee per day.
- Check-out only after check-in.
- Work duration equals check-out minus check-in.
- Under five hours counts as a half day.
- No attendance record on a working day means absent.

Implement these rules consistently.

For attendance displays, use clearly labeled statuses:
- Present.
- Late.
- Half day.
- Absent.
- Not checked out.

If an employee has checked in but not checked out, show that state accurately rather than inventing completed working hours.

### Working days

Use the configured company working-day settings consistently when calculating absences and payroll.

Do not count a configured non-working day as an ordinary absence.

Use one consistent date strategy to avoid records being assigned to the wrong day because of timezone conversion.

