# 11. PAYSLIP AND PRINTING

Build a polished monthly payslip page.

Display:
- Company name.
- Payslip period.
- Employee name.
- Employee email or ID.
- Department.
- Monthly salary.
- Working days in the month.
- Absent days.
- Half days.
- Per-day salary.
- Attendance deduction.
- Net salary.

Use the exact calculation rules from the Beginner Track brief.

### Required formulas

Per-day salary:

`monthly salary ÷ working days in the month`

Deduction:

`per-day salary × (absent days + 0.5 × half days)`

Net salary:

`monthly salary − deduction`

The Beginner Track does not specify tax calculations. Do not import the advanced-track tax slabs into this version.

Handle zero working days safely and use sensible rounding for displayed money.

### Printing

Use a dedicated print stylesheet.

When the user clicks Print / Save as PDF:
- Hide the sidebar and navigation.
- Hide unnecessary controls.
- Display the payslip cleanly on a white background.
- Prevent important information from being clipped.
- Keep the printed document professional and readable.

Use the browser's native print dialog. Do not claim to have generated a downloadable PDF file unless an actual PDF-generation implementation exists.

Admin may view employee payslips. Employees may access only their own.

